  [PASS] DRAFT is editable
  [PASS] ISSUED is not
  [PASS] ACCEPTED is not
  [PASS] REJECTED is not
  [PASS] EXPIRED is not
  [PASS] SUPERSEDED is not

── E3. an accepted quotation cannot be revised, but a lapsed one can 
  [PASS] ISSUED is revisable
  [PASS] EXPIRED is revisable
  [PASS] REJECTED is revisable
  [PASS] ACCEPTED is NOT — it is what the customer agreed to
  [PASS] nor is a SUPERSEDED one

── E4. illegal transitions are refused with an explanation ───────
  [PASS] a draft cannot be accepted without being issued
  [PASS] an accepted quotation cannot be un-accepted
  [PASS] and the message says what to do instead
  [PASS] and does not send them to revise an accepted quotation, which is refused
  [PASS] issuing twice is refused as already-done, not as illegal
  [PASS] and the legal move is not refused

── E5. expiry is a comparison against the validity date, both ways 
  [PASS] a quote valid until yesterday has expired
  [PASS] one valid until tomorrow has not
  [PASS] and one with no validity date never expires

